      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to State Government"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The State Executive consists of the Governor, Chief Minister, and Council of Ministers.",
        "The State Legislature encompasses the Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha) and Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad).",
        "Constitutional Articles define the specific powers, duties, and structures governing state administration.",
        "Understanding the division of authority between the Governor and the Chief Minister is central to state governance."
      ],
      "id": "2jfdp5s"
